      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-282538",
      ":question/problem": "A company pays $$75$ to manufacture a smartphone. A sales agent earns a commission equal to $15%$ of the sales price of the smartphone. The company\u2019s profit on each phone is the sales price minus both the production cost and the commission. If the sales price of the phone is $$120$, which of the following equations gives the number of units, $n$, the company sold to earn a profit of $$8,250$?"
